{"type":"message","id":"10a3e905","parentId":"564df6f2","timestamp":"2026-03-27T14:11:06.453Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_ewifzuoibazr_1","toolName":"coze_web_search","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Coze web search: crypto bitcoin price today March 27 2026 fear greed index\n\nResults (5)\n1. Bitcoin Fear &     Greed Index Hits All-Time Low of 5 in 2026 — What History Says Happens Next\n   URL: https://cryptonewsbytes.com/bitcoin-fear-greed-index-all-time-low-2026/\n   Source: Cryptonewsbytes\n   Published: 2026-02-17T00:00:00+08:00\n   Most Fearful Moment in Bitcoin’s History\n⚡ What You Need to Know\nThe Bitcoin Fear & Greed Index hit \n2. Crypto Fear and Greed Index Hits All-Time Low Amid Huge Bitcoin Crash\n   URL: https://99bitcoins.com/news/presales/crypto-fear-and-greed-6-year-low-bitcoin-crash/\n   Source: 99Bitcoins\n   Published: 2026-02-06T00:00:00+08:00\n   axi Doge (MAXI) Presale Amid this Brutal Crypto Crash?\nCrypto sentiment has dropped to its lowest le\n3. Data: The current Crypto Fear and Greed Index is 24, indicating an extreme fear state.\n   URL: https://www.bitget.com/news/detail/12560605279285\n   Source: Bitget\n   Published: 2026-03-19T12:32:00+08:00\n   Data: The current Crypto Fear and Greed Index is 24, indicating an extreme fear state.\nChaincatcher\n\n4. Data: The current Crypto Fear and Greed Index is 13, indicating an extreme fear state.\n   URL: https://www.bitget.online/news/detail/12560605247001\n   Source: Bitget\n   Published: 2026-03-08T12:32:00+08:00\n   Data: The current Crypto Fear and Greed Index is 13, indicating an extreme fear state.\nChaincatcher\n\n5. Trending news\n   URL: https://www.bitget.online/news/detail/12560605264796\n   Source: Bitget\n   Published: 2026-03-14T14:15:00+08:00\n   Data: The current Crypto Fear & Greed Index is 15, indicating an extreme fear state.\nChaincatcher\n20"}],"details":{"query":"crypto bitcoin price today March 27 2026 fear greed index","type":"web","count":5,"items":[{"title":"Bitcoin Fear &     Greed Index Hits All-Time Low of 5 in 2026 — What History Says Happens Next","url":"https://cryptonewsbytes.com/bitcoin-fear-greed-index-all-time-low-2026/","siteName":"Cryptonewsbytes","snippet":"Most Fearful Moment in Bitcoin’s History\n⚡ What You Need to Know\nThe Bitcoin Fear & Greed Index hit ","content":"Bitcoin\nBitcoin Fear & Greed Index Hits All-Time Low of 5 in 2026 — What History Says Happens Next\nAuthor : Aaron\nFebruary 17, 2026\nTable of Contents\n⚡ What You Need to Know\nBitcoin Fear & Greed Index Hits All-Time Low of 5 in 2026 — The Complete Data-Driven Analysis\nEvery Major Bitcoin Crash: Fear & Greed Index Compared\nWhat Caused the Fear Index to Hit 5 in February 2026?\nThe 7-Day Crash Timeline\nWhat On-Chain Data Shows — The Signal Behind the Fear\n📊 Key On-Chain Signals — February 2026\nCrash-by-Crash History: What Came After Each Extreme Fear Reading\n2012 Crash — Index: 10 | BTC: $7.08 → Next Peak: $1,100 (+15,400%)\nMt. Gox Crash — Index: 9 | BTC: $421.57 → Next Peak: $19,500 (+4,526%)\n2017–18 Bear Market — Index: 11 | BTC: $3,129 → Next Peak: $69,000 (+2,104%)\nCovid Crash — Index: 9 | BTC: $3,852 → Next Peak: $69,000 (+1,691%)\nFTX Crash — Index: 12 | BTC: $15,642 → Next Peak: $126,000 (+806%)\nWhat Major Analysts Are Saying About the 2026 Crash\nWhy 2026 Is Different — And Why That Matters for Investors\nThe Three Key Differences\n🐂 Bull Case\n🐻 Bear Case\nHow to Navigate Extreme Fear: Evidence-Based Strategies\n📈 The Dollar-Cost Averaging (DCA) Framework\nFrequently Asked Questions\nConclusion: Reading the Most Fearful Moment in Bitcoin’s History\n⚡ What You Need to Know\nThe Bitcoin Fear & Greed Index hit 5 on February 6, 2026 — the lowest reading in the index’s recorded history, lower than FTX (12), Covid (9), Mt. Gox (9), and the 2017–18 crash (11)\nBitcoin was priced at $59,948 at peak fear — the highest crash floor ever recorded at extreme fear levels, having fallen 52% from its $126,000 all-time high\n$2.6 billion in leveraged positions were liquidated in 24 hours; Open Interest collapsed from $103B to $61B; ETF outflows exceeded $816M in two days\nOn-chain data tells a different story: Glassnode’s Accumulation Trend Score hit 0.68 — wallets holding 10–100 BTC were the most aggressive dip buyers, and 66,940 BTC moved into accumulation wallets on February 6 alone\nEvery prior extreme fear reading (below 12) was followed by gains of 806% to 15,400% in the next cycle — but recovery timelines ranged from 13 months to 24 months\nKey risk: unlike previous crashes, this one has no single trigger, and institutions are net sellers — breaking the pattern seen at every prior major bottom\nBitcoin Fear & Greed Index Hits All-Time Low of 5 in 2026 — The Complete Data-Driven Analysis\nOn February 6, 2026, something that had never happened before in Bitcoin’s 17-year history occurred: the Crypto Fear & Greed Index dropped to 5 out of 100. [CCN] Not 12, like during the FTX collapse. Not 9, like during the Covid crash. Not 6, like during the Terra/Luna meltdown. Five. The single lowest reading since the index was created — in the same week Bitcoin was still trading near $60,000.\nA viral Reddit post showing side-by-side Fear & Greed gauge readings from every major Bitcoin crash crystallised what the raw data shows: the 2026 crash has produced deeper fear than any event in crypto history, at a price floor that would have been an all-time high just three years ago.\nBut sentiment data is only one layer of this story. Underneath the fear readings sits a body of on-chain evidence — from Glassnode, CryptoQuant, and Santiment — that paints a more nuanced picture of who is actually buying, who is selling, and what has historically come next. This is the complete analysis.\n5\nFear Index Low (Feb 6)\n$59,948\nBTC at Peak Fear\n$2.6B\nLiquidations in 24hrs\n0.68\nGlassnode Accum. Score\nEvery Major Bitcoin Crash: Fear & Greed Index Compared\nThe index has only recorded single-digit readings on a handful of occasions across Bitcoin’s entire history. Here is every major crash event with its corresponding fear reading and Bitcoin price at the moment of maximum fear:\n2012 Crash\n10\nExtreme Fear\n$7.08\n▼ 4.1% (24h)\nMt. Gox Crash\n9\nExtreme Fear\n$421.57\n▼ 8.9% (24h)\n’17–18 Crash\n11\nExtreme Fear\n$3,129.39\n▼ 2.1% (24h)\nCovid Crash\n9\nExtreme Fear\n$3,852.65\n▼ 6.3% (24h)\nFTX Crash\n12\nExtreme Fear\n$15,642.12\n▼ 4.8% (24h)\n⚡ ALL-TIME LOW\n2026 Crash\n5\nExtreme Fear\n$59,948.39\n▼ 3.9% (24h)\nThe pattern is stark. Every previous crash floor hit a lower price with a higher fear reading. The 2026 reading of 5 arrived with Bitcoin near $60,000 — a price that represented a cycle all-time high just three years prior. This is the defining data point of the current market moment: maximum fear at a historically unprecedented price floor.\nCrash Fear Index BTC at Fear Low Next Cycle Peak Max Gain Recovery Time\n2012 10 $7.08 $1,100 +15,400% ~18 months\nMt. Gox 2014 9 $421.57 $19,500 +4,526% ~36 months\n2017–18 Bear 11 $3,129.39 $69,000 +2,104% ~24 months\nCovid Mar 2020 9 $3,852.65 $69,000 +1,691% ~13 months\nFTX Nov 2022 12 $15,642.12 $126,000 +806% ~18 months\n⚡ 2026 (Feb 6) 5 — Record $59,948.39 ??? TBD TBD\nWhat Caused the Fear Index to Hit 5 in February 2026?\nUnlike previous crashes that had single identifiable triggers — FTX’s fraud, Covid-19 panic, the Mt. Gox hack — the 2026 crash is the result of multiple headwinds converging simultaneously. Understanding what drove fear to its historic low is essential to assessing whether the usual historical playbook applies.\nThe 7-Day Crash Timeline\nJanuary 31, 2026\nBitcoin breaks $83,000 support — first warning\nBitcoin lost 7.3%, dropping to $82,700. Glassnode  data showed BTC consolidating just above structural support at $83,400 — the lower bound of the short-term holder cost basis model. Long-term holders began selling at the fastest pace since August 2025. [CoinDesk]\nFebruary 4, 2026\nFear & Greed drops to 11 — ETF outflows begin\nThe index fell to 11 as Bitcoin and Ethereum each dropped over 7%. More than $800 million in leveraged positions were liquidated in 24 hours. Open Interest fell to $103 billion. Bitcoin ETFs saw $545 million in outflows — the start of a two-day withdrawal exceeding $816 million total. [CoinDesk]\nFebruary 5, 2026\nBitcoin drops below $61,000 — $1.26B liquidated in one day\nBitcoin briefly fell below $61,000, liquidating over $1.26 billion in positions in a single session and erasing $2 trillion from the total crypto market cap. The Fear & Greed Index hit 9 — a multi-year low at the time. Options markets showed peak fear with put premiums over 10 points above calls on Deribit. [CCN]\nFebruary 6, 2026 — ⚡ ALL-TIME LOW\nFear & Greed hits 5 — the most fearful day in Bitcoin history\nThe index hit 5, surpassing the Terra/Luna low of 6 (June 2022) and every previous extreme fear reading. Bitcoin’s daily RSI dropped to 15.64 — below March 2020, below the Covid crash. Over $2.6 billion in leveraged positions were liquidated in 24 hours total. Simultaneously, Glassnode data showed 66,940 BTC moving into accumulation wallets — a massive divergence between sentiment and on-chain behaviour. [Blockzeit]\nFebruary 7–14, 2026\nAccumulation emerges — relief rally begins\nBitcoin accumulation broadened across all cohorts for the first time since late November 2025. Wallets holding 10–100 BTC were the most aggressive dip buyers. Glassnode’s Accumulation Trend Score climbed to 0.68. Spot Bitcoin ETFs recorded three consecutive days of inflows totalling hundreds of millions — led by ARK & 21Shares, BlackRock’s IBIT, and Fidelity. [CoinDesk]\nWhat On-Chain Data Shows — The Signal Behind the Fear\nSentiment indices measure how people feel. On-chain data measures what they do. In February 2026, those two signals pointed in dramatically different directions — and historically, on-chain behaviour has been the more reliable predictor of what comes next.\n📊 Key On-Chain Signals — February 2026\nGlassnode Accumulation Trend Score: 0.68 — The highest reading since November 2025, signalling coordinated buying across wallet cohorts, not isolated large purchases. A score above 0.5 indicates broad-based accumulation. [Coinmonks]\n66,940 BTC moved into accumulation wallets on February 6 — the same day fear hit 5. Wallets holding 10,000–100,000 BTC accumulated over 70,000 BTC in early February. At ~$67,000 per BTC, that equals $4.6 billion in fresh exposure from large capital allocators.\nSOPR (Spent Output Profit Ratio) below 1.0 — Since mid-January 2026, SOPR has hovered at or below 1, meaning sellers are realising losses. This phase is known as capitulation — it historically marks structural exhaustion of sellers, not the start of further decline. The same SOPR pattern appeared before the 2018, 2020, and 2022 recoveries. [Coinmonks]\nMVRV Adaptive Z-Score: -2.66 — CryptoQuant contributor GugaOnChain described this as “consistent with persistent capitulation” and noted the indicator suggests “approaching the historical accumulation phase.” This Z-Score level has coincided with major market lows in previous cycles. [Bitbo]\nBitcoin daily RSI: 15.64 — Below March 2020’s Covid crash reading. Below every comparable panic event in Bitcoin’s history. An RSI this low has never been sustained for more than a few weeks before a significant mean-reversion bounce.\nThe divergence between record-low sentiment and record-high accumulation activity is significant. As on-chain analysts have repeatedly identified at major Bitcoin turning points, when retail panic and whale accumulation diverge this sharply, the historical resolution has consistently favoured the accumulators over the panic sellers — though the timeline for that resolution has varied considerably.\nCrash-by-Crash History: What Came After Each Extreme Fear Reading\n2012 Crash — Index: 10 | BTC: $7.08 → Next Peak: $1,100 (+15,400%)\nBitcoin’s first major fear event came amid regulatory uncertainty and exchange collapses. The index hitting 10 with Bitcoin at $7.08 looked like the end of a failed experiment to most observers. By late 2013, Bitcoin had reached $1,100. The lesson: early-cycle extreme fear at low prices produced the most asymmetric return profile in Bitcoin’s history — but required a patient hold of 12–18 months.\nMt. Gox Crash — Index: 9 | BTC: $421.57 → Next Peak: $19,500 (+4,526%)\nThe Mt. Gox collapse in 20...","publishTime":"2026-02-17T00:00:00+08:00"},{"title":"Crypto Fear and Greed Index Hits All-Time Low Amid Huge Bitcoin Crash","url":"https://99bitcoins.com/news/presales/crypto-fear-and-greed-6-year-low-bitcoin-crash/","siteName":"99Bitcoins","snippet":"axi Doge (MAXI) Presale Amid this Brutal Crypto Crash?\nCrypto sentiment has dropped to its lowest le","content":"Presales News\nCrypto Fear and Greed Index Hits All-Time Low Amid Huge Bitcoin Crash\nBy Alex Ioannou\nLast Updated: February 6, 2026\nIn This Article\nWhat Does Crypto Extreme Fear and Greed Really Mean?\nWhy Macro Pressure Is Crushing Bitcoin, Sparking Huge Crypto Crash\nBONUS: Why are Investors Seeking Safety in the Maxi Doge (MAXI) Presale Amid this Brutal Crypto Crash?\nCrypto sentiment has dropped to its lowest level in around six years, with the crypto fear and greed index dropping to 4/100 overnight, a level not seen since the COVID crash in March 2020. It comes as the Bitcoin  price slid to around $60,255, a 15-month low, wiping out more than half its value since late 2025.\nThe selloff reflects a wider squeeze from Fed policy uncertainty, a stronger dollar, and the US circling Iran, resulting in fading risk appetite across global markets.\nCrypto Fear and Greed Chart\nFGI\nBTC Price\n0\n20\n40\n60\n80\n100\n$0.00\n$20.00k\n$40.00k\n$60.00k\n$80.00k\n$100.00k\n$120.00k\n$140.00k\nFeb 2025\nApr 2025\nMay 2025\nJun 2025\nAug 2025\nSep 2025\nOct 2025\nDec 2025\nJan 2026\nFeb 2026\nBTC Price\nFGI\nThe fear level now mirrors the mood of both the 2022 FTX Exchange collapse and the March 2020 COVID crash, a two-year period that drained billions from the market and left thousands of investors financially ruined, with the scars still present today.\nCurrent price action hasn’t been helped by the likes of BlackRock, whose IBIT Bitcoin ETF has seen over $400M in outflows over the past two days, adding more sell pressure to an already struggling market.\nWhat Does Crypto Extreme Fear and Greed Really Mean?\nThe Crypto Fear & Greed Index dropped to 4/100 overnight, an unprecedented level, but has since rallied to 9/100. Both 4 and 9 mark “Extreme Fear.” It works by combining price moves, volatility, and trading behavior into a single number that indicates how investors feel about current market conditions.\nHistorically, whenever the index falls into the single digits, it signals panic selling. Although this is when investors can feel at their lowest, watching their bags dwindle to nothing, smart players watch these moments because forced selling can push prices far below fair value.\nThe last time fear hit this level was during two separate occasions in 2022. First, the Terra Luna unwinding in May, followed by the FTX Exchange collapse in November. Those crashes broke confidence after the Terra UST stablecoin lost its dollar peg, resulting in billions of dollars in retail investment going up in smoke.\nA reported $200Bn was lost as the Sam Bankman-Fried-led FTX Exchange collapsed later in 2022, which capped off a rough year for crypto market participants after seemingly endless black swan events.\nPrior to this was the March 2020 COVID crash, which saw the Bitcoin price drop by -50% in a few hours. Now, six years on from COVID and four from the FTX/Terra collapse, we’re back here again.\nBitcoin\nBTC\n$69,085.09\n1.13% 24h\nMarket Cap\n$1380.72836B\nWhy Macro Pressure Is Crushing Bitcoin, Sparking Huge Crypto Crash\nThis Bitcoin crash and broader crypto market downturn come as a rising US dollar tightens financial conditions, making risky assets less attractive. The Dollar Index has jumped since late January, pulling liquidity out of the cryptocurrency market.\nThen there is the US and its latest war efforts, this time with Iran. Tensions are growing in the region as talks have reportedly stalled, and a full-scale invasion of the Middle-Eastern nation could spell further disaster for crypto.\nThis broad macro squeeze explains the crypto crash despite growing adoption and ETF access. In fact, the emergence of crypto ETFs is having a negative effect on the charts right now. BlackRock is leading the way in negative flows, dumping over $550M in BTC USD over the past few days.\nRecord breaking trading volume for U.S. 🇺🇸 Bitcoin ETFs 👇 $IBIT  over $7.3 Billion 💥 pic.twitter.com/kThu3bNhDq\nWhen things are going well, positive flows into ETF products help stabilize prices and drive them higher, but in times of uncertainty, institutional investors seek safety, and their dumping of Bitcoin through these products only adds to the already heavy sell pressure.\nEverywhere we look, crypto is bleeding, from the major caps such as Bitcoin and Ethereum, down to the lowliest of meme coins. Could Maxi Doge (MAXI)  be just what investors are looking for in these trying times?\nThis new crypto meme coin presale has raised over $4.5M in funding to date and is quietly becoming one of the most in-demand projects in 2026.\nBONUS: Why are Investors Seeking Safety in the Maxi Doge (MAXI) Presale Amid this Brutal Crypto Crash?\nPut simply, investors want to feel something again. Long gone are the days of the community running the likes of DOGE, SHIB, and PEPE to billions, printing overnight millionaires in the process. With the Crypto greed and fear index hitting unprecedented lows, crypto needs a saviour now more than ever.\nMAXI is speaking to this nostalgia, branded as a ‘DOGE on steroids’, this is the next generation of meme coin, with all of the memes and community spirit that raised Dogecoin and others to their current levels, but with built-in staking initiatives that help take Maxi Doge to the next level.\nAnother factor driving investors into the MAXI presale is that the token isn’t live yet and, as such, isn’t at the mercy of the ongoing crypto crash. This means traders can simply park their funds in the Maxi Doge presale and kick back, waiting for it to close.\nIf the MAXI token launches at a better time in the market, it could be the golden lottery ticket for investors in 2026. Be part of the Maxi Doge community by joining the degens on X and Telegram, and stay up to date with all things MAXI.\n#Presales\n","publishTime":"2026-02-06T00:00:00+08:00"},{"title":"Data: The current Crypto Fear and Greed Index is 24, indicating an extreme fear state.","url":"https://www.bitget.com/news/detail/12560605279285","siteName":"Bitget","snippet":"Data: The current Crypto Fear and Greed Index is 24, indicating an extreme fear state.\nChaincatcher\n","content":"Data: The current Crypto Fear and Greed Index is 24, indicating an extreme fear state.\nChaincatcher\n2026/03/19 12:32\nChainCatcher news, according to Coinglass data, the current cryptocurrency Fear and Greed Index is 24, down 3 points from yesterday. The 7-day average is 20, and the 30-day average is 13.\n","publishTime":"2026-03-19T12:32:00+08:00"},{"title":"Data: The current Crypto Fear and Greed Index is 13, indicating an extreme fear state.","url":"https://www.bitget.online/news/detail/12560605247001","siteName":"Bitget","snippet":"Data: The current Crypto Fear and Greed Index is 13, indicating an extreme fear state.\nChaincatcher\n","content":"Data: The current Crypto Fear and Greed Index is 13, indicating an extreme fear state.\nChaincatcher\n2026/03/08 12:32\nChainCatcher news, according to Coinglass data, the current cryptocurrency Fear & Greed Index is 13, up 0 points from yesterday. The 7-day average is 14, and the 30-day average is 10.\n","publishTime":"2026-03-08T12:32:00+08:00"},{"title":"Trending news","url":"https://www.bitget.online/news/detail/12560605264796","siteName":"Bitget","snippet":"Data: The current Crypto Fear & Greed Index is 15, indicating an extreme fear state.\nChaincatcher\n20","content":"Data: The current Crypto Fear & Greed Index is 15, indicating an extreme fear state.\nChaincatcher\n2026/03/14 14:15\nChainCatcher news, according to Coinglass data, the current cryptocurrency Fear and Greed Index is 15, up 1 point from yesterday. The 7-day average is 13, and the 30-day average is 11.\n","publishTime":"2026-03-14T14:15:00+08:00"}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774620666451}}
